# Everything on the site: any http:// picture, sound or request a page asks for
# (a profile photo, a cover, a song, a link preview from somewhere that still
# hands out http links) is fetched as https:// instead. One insecure resource
# is enough for Chrome to call the whole page "not secure" even with a valid
# certificate; this makes that impossible without touching each source.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: upgrade-insecure-requests

/stickers/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
